  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Risk-based Child Labour Monitoring and Remediation System in Cameroon</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">This project contributed to identify, prevent and address child labour in Cargill&#x2019;s cocoa supply chain in Cameroon. To achieve this, Cargill, Telcar and the International Cocoa Initiative (ICI) worked together to establish a risk-based Child Labour Monitoring and Remediation System (CLMRS). The CLMRS allows a more efficient and faster identification of child labour incidents, assign the necessary remediation activities, and prevent future cases by addressing the root causes. The project reached more than 50,000 producers and their families in Cargill-Telcar&#x2019;s cocoa supply chain in Cameroon living in 1,146 communities.Cargill and ICI continued working together to monitor new farmers, remediate identified cases of child labour and children at risk, and conduct prevention activities through income diversification for women. The project was implemented in a period of two years (2021-2023) after which Cargill-Telcar consolidated a due diligence system in its supply chain in Cameroon, integrating and scaling up the CLMRS to identify, remediate and prevent child labour. Cargill-Telcar will also address the adverse impacts of supply chain on labour issues. The proposed risk-based CLMRS approach will allow Cargill to continuously monitor child labour and remediate child labour cases even after the end of this project, expecting a gradual reduction of child labour rates. The project included the following activity areas: 1.	Targeted remediation for child labour cases: remediation activities to identified child labour cases to be implemented by Cargill and/or local partners at household and community levels. 2.	Prevention through increased income: income generating activities for women will be supported to increase the income of cocoa households and therefore prevent child labour. 3.	Risk-based child labour monitoring: monitoring system based on predefined risk factors in Cargill&#x2019;s cocoa supply chain to identify child labour cases through data collection and raise awareness at household, farm, and community levels. 4.	A due diligence system: following recommendations to address adverse impacts of supply chain operations on labour issues in the supply chain such as forced labour, grievance mechanisms, traceability, etc.</narrative>
  </description>
